# Review: user interface guidelines

Read **User interface guidelines** in `doc/architecture.rst` before
reviewing a UI change. That section is the source of truth, including
Screen rectangles and Touch interaction. Do not invent a parallel
colour, gesture, or layout rule. If this file and the section
disagree, the section wins.

## Reject

- A new colour role, or a raw `Color(0x..)` outside Look
  `Initialise()`. Red is a warning and wants a sound. Orange is a
  caution. Green means OK. An advisory is neither red nor green.
  InfoBox blue is derived or pending, not a safety colour.
- Text or chrome that follows `UISettings::DarkMode` is readable with
  dark mode off and on. Pass that flag into Look `Initialise()`.
  InfoBoxes may follow the global mode, or stay Light or Dark. Kobo
  stays light. Use the named colours in `Look/Colors.hpp`.
- A control whose name or result differs from the same control in an
  InfoBox, menu, dialogue, or status line.
- An in-flight action more than three steps from `mode=default`, or a
  rare option placed on the flying screen instead of Setup.
- Menu timeout (`UISettings::menu_timeout`) applied to a warning.
- An action left enabled when it cannot be done. A destructive action
  that does not ask, and does not say what will be lost.
- A gesture or long press with no label. Touch that commits on press
  instead of lift-off. See `.cursor/rules/ui-touch.mdc`.
- An in-flight target smaller than `Layout::GetInflightButtonHeight()`
  (about 20 mm). Dialogue rows that ignore
  `Layout::GetMinimumControlHeight()`.
- Type sized for the wrong distance. Auto shrinks type when the short
  edge is under 3.2 inches. Handheld always uses that closer-view
  size. Panel keeps full-size type for arm's length. Use
  `Layout::FontScale()` and `Layout::VptScale()`.
- A widget in the wrong screen rectangle, or map chrome drawn on the
  ownship symbol.
- An e-paper path (`HasEPaper()`, `IsDithered()`) that needs colour,
  a gradient, or a timer `Invalidate()` when the pixels did not change.
